.TH AGENT-WATCH 1 "2026-09-09" "agent-watcher" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-watch \- notify which agent tab needs input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-watch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-watch
is a daemon that watches coding agents and emits a desktop notification
naming the exact workspace/tab/agent that needs attention, so you know which
tab to look at when several agents or LLM harnesses are running at once.
.PP
It has two sources:
.TP
.B herdr
Polls \fBherdr api snapshot\fR and notifies when a background (non-focused)
agent pane transitions to a needs-attention state: \fBblocked\fR (approval or
question UI), \fBdone\fR (background work finished), or \fBidle\fR while
unfocused (ready for input).
.TP
.B external
Finds known coding-agent processes running outside herdr (controlling tty not
owned by a herdr pane) and notifies when one appears and its terminal goes
idle. Best-effort heuristic; unvalidated against a live standalone instance.
.PP
The pane you are already looking at is skipped, and notifications are
deduplicated per episode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-herdr-bin \fIPATH\fR
Path to the herdr CLI (default: \fBherdr\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-notify-cmd \fICMD\fR
Notification command (default: \fBnotify-send\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR
herdr poll interval (default: 2.0).
.TP
.B \-\-external-interval \fISECONDS\fR
External scan interval (default: 5.0).
.TP
.B \-\-idle-threshold \fISECONDS\fR
External tty idle seconds before "needs input" (default: 10.0).
.TP
.B \-\-once
Single pass, then exit (for smoke tests).
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print notifications instead of sending them.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Print what it would notify right now
.B agent-watch \-\-once \-\-dry-run
.TP
Send one real pass of notifications
.B agent-watch \-\-once
.TP
Poll faster
.B agent-watch \-\-interval 1
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/projects/agent-watcher/agent-watch
The daemon source.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/agent-watch.service
The systemd user unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR herdr (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the Oh My Pi harness user.
